      "title": "Routing topology is configuration, not a time series",
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 56,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The routing topology (which backends exist, their weights, and the fallback chain) is **configuration**, not a metric. Read it live from the router itself:\n\n```\nGET /v1/router/summary\n```\n\nThat endpoint returns the currently effective router configuration the SCM-supervised process loaded. The panels above show what that configuration is *doing* (attempts, errors, latency, fallbacks); the endpoint shows what it *is*. A config change is a discrete event, and this board does not record config history."
      }
